@0    = ~I don't get it, I really don't.~
@1    = ~Oh? Is there some problem?~
@2    = ~This. This whole thing with <CHARNAME>. C'mon, Angelo, surely you can see this is getting...~
@3    = ~Well, you know...~
@4    = ~Please, friend. Carry on. I wouldn't want you to hold yourself back, heh.~
@5    = ~...mid-life-crisis...~
@6    = ~I don't believe I need to explain myself to anyone but the lady in question. Especially not some pup who thinks he's a man of the world just because he's had a pipe or two of Black Lotus.~
@7    = ~Oh, come on, that's not fair.~
@8    = ~You have your whole life ahead of you. Dozens of serving wenches - or, heh, strapping waiters, if that's what you go for.~
@9    = ~Hells, I know how you feel: I've felt it myself, many a time. If you want another notch on your bedpost, you can get it somewhere else.~
@10   = ~You've made me a happier man than I could have dreamed. Six months ago, I would never have thought I could travel with such a--~
@11   = ~Can you hear yourself? You just want her because she killed your old boss. You're getting all maudlin over her when you've known her all of a--~
@12   = ~Do you think I don't know she deserves better than me?~
@13   = ~Damn straight she does. Hell if I'd go with a guy who tried to kill me.~
@14   = ~It's her choice. Let me have my happiness, if she deems me worthy.~
@15   = ~Oh, yeah, and if she doesn't?~
@16   = ~Then I am unluckier than I thought.~
@17   = ~Faren, I think of you as a friend, but I don't feel anything more.~
@18   = ~Angelo, I don't know why you think I deserve better than you. I want you.~
@19   = ~Faren's right. I think I do deserve something better.~
@20   = ~I can't say how much it means to hear you say it, <CHARNAME>. I'll do my best to help you be happy.~
@21   = ~Don't come running to me when he robs you blind and leaves you in a gutter somewhere.~
@22   = ~I think there are words for that, Faren - sour grapes. Now I think <CHARNAME> and I had something to discuss...~
@23   = ~Well, at least you know I'm not going to sell you out to the highest bidder.~
@24   = ~I would never have done that, <CHARNAME>. I hope you understand that. Excuse me.~
@25   = ~Heheh, you're a funny one, aren't you? Drifting around, doing a bit of this and that to make ends meet. You remind me of myself at your age.~
@26   = ~Except I don't go around helping murderous Bhaalspawn start wars up in the north.~
@27   = ~Ho-ho! Holier-than-thou, now, is it? Much good may it do you, friend. If our <PRO_LADYLORD> <CHARNAME> can afford to leave such things behind, I'm sure you can, too.~
@28   = ~No, no, no. You've got to feed them the Black Lotus first. That makes them more...pliable. Talkative.~
@29   = ~But then they'll get too sleepy, and you won't get anything useful out of them.~
@30   = ~Sleepy means comfortable, and in the long run it'll hurt them less than beating them up.~
@31   = ~I guess so.~
@32   = ~Ugh, I'm glad I'm out of all that stuff.~
@33   = ~Me too, Faren. Me too.~
@34   = ~Ten gold pieces says she's a virgin.~
@35   = ~No way. Look at the way she's walking.~
@36   = ~Heh heh, look closer. No woman pouts as much as that if she knows just what she's flaunting. Oh, if I were ten years younger...~
@37   = ~I don't believe you. You want me to ask her?~
@38   = ~Tsh, man. It'll take all the fun out of guessing.~
